      "title": "6105 Final Shaving Accommodation (Enlisted)",
      "description": "Final 6105 counseling at twelve months of clean-shaven medical accommodation for an enlisted Marine: MEB referral, AA Form extension request, separation under MCO 1900.16 para 6203.2 with RE-3P (MARADMIN 348/26).",
      "documentType": "page11"
    }
  },
  "data": {
    "formData": {
      "documentType": "page11",
      "name": "",
      "edipi": "",
      "date": "",
      "remarksLeft": "[YYYYMMDD]: Counseled this date concerning the following deficiencies: inability to comply with clean-shaven grooming standards established in MCO 1020.34H and having reached 12 consecutive months of treatment requiring a medical accommodation.\n\nThe accommodation was approved by the commanding officer on [YYYYMMDD] and documented on NAVMC 11830. The accommodation will expire [YYYYMMDD], which is twelve months from the date of approval.\n\nMarines requiring a clean-shaven grooming accommodation due to a medical condition for more than twelve months will be evaluated for administrative separation under MCO 1900.16, paragraph 6203.2, (Convenience of the Government, Condition Not a Disability), and if separated will be assigned a reenlistment code of RE-3P.\n\nGrooming Standards: You must strictly maintain facial hair length not to exceed one quarter of an inch (0.25) in length.\n\nSpecific recommendations for corrective action are to continue to comply fully with the prescribed medical treatment plan, to attend all scheduled medical evaluations and re-evaluations as appropriate. You will receive a formal referral to a Medical Evaluation Board (MEB) to document whether your condition constitutes a physical disability under the Disability Evaluation System (DES).\n\nYou shall submit an Administrative Action Form (NAVMC 10274) requesting an administrative extension to the clean-shaven accommodation while the MEB and separation proceedings are pending.\n\nYou shall carry a copy of your expired NAVMC 11830 along with a copy of your submitted AA Form or DC M&RA approved extension at all times and present as requested.\n\nI understand that failure to complete my enlistment contract with an honorable characterization of service may preclude my eligibility for benefits from the Department of Veterans Affairs or other organizations and have an adverse effect on future civilian employment.\n\nI was advised that within 5 working days after acknowledging this entry I may submit a written rebuttal which will be filed in my official military personnel file (OMPF).\n\nI choose to ____ / not to ____ make such a statement.\n\n\n_____________________          _____________________\nSignature of Marine            Signature of Commanding Officer",
      "remarksRight": ""
    },
